# Operator tooling lives here. It runs against real credentials, so the rules
# below exist to stop a local convenience file becoming a committed secret.
#
# Generated output already has its own rules in whatsapp-templates/out/ and
# whatsapp-flows/out/ — this file covers the ad-hoc things that land at the top
# level of scripts/ while someone is working.

# Any environment file, whatever the suffix. The root .gitignore only lists the
# specific names it expects at the repo root; a scripts/.env.staging would slip
# straight through it.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Python. Nothing in this service is Python — the one file that was
# (create_listpickers.py, a Twilio Content list-picker creator) outlived its
# feature and was removed. Anything reappearing here is a local scratch tool,
# and those have a habit of holding an API key in a variable at the top.
*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Ad-hoc one-off scripts. The convention is a `_tmp-` or `_local-` prefix for
# anything you do not intend to commit, so it can be written next to the module
# it imports without being staged by a wide `git add`.
_tmp-*
_local-*
*.local.ts

# Command output someone piped to a file mid-debug. dump-twilio-config.ts in
# particular prints live credentials to stdout.
*.log
*.out
dump-*.txt
